        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After going back and forth with this, I think adding extra care for horizontal view is a good thing. So this should now be resolved on latest `main`.\n\nSaving and restoring the horizontal view (more precisely, its left column) is both the most robust way of doing it (unlike three-quarter-measure of temporarily setting `sidescroll=0` as described in neovim/neovim#32966) while being decently fast (both `winsaveview` and `winrestview` with only `leftcol` takes couple of *micro*seconds on my intermediately performant laptop, which should be good enough).\n\nThanks again for noticing this!",
